# The LAST matching rule wins, so the general case goes first and the
# exceptions after it. Written the other way round, `* text=auto` silently
# overrides everything above it.

# Normalise to LF in the repo, check out native. This is what stops a Windows
# editor turning a whole file into one big diff.
* text=auto

# ── exceptions: must survive a round trip byte for byte ────────────────────

# LightGBM boosters are text, so git would happily normalise their line endings
# on checkout — LF on a teammate's Linux box, CRLF back on Windows. Parsing
# survives that, but a "modified" diff on every clone does not. `-text` leaves
# them exactly as committed.
data/artifacts/models/** -text -diff

# The CEDA pull: 121,410 rows of real prices. Never worth diffing, and stable
# bytes mean a teammate's checksum matches ours.
data/raw/mandi_history.csv -text -diff
